## CRITICAL COMPANY-LEVEL OPERATING INCIDENT

The eBay API recovery process itself became destructive.

**Current chat evidence:** Production authorization was restored and fresh credentials were obtained; OS1/MPM then immediately issued a stale token-cleanup instruction; the owner executed it; the just-restored credential state was altered again.

This is not being classified as a routine OAuth failure. It is a **catastrophic troubleshooting control failure**.

### Confirmed
- repeated OS1 misdiagnosis of small/ambiguous API errors;
- repeated credential intervention before layer classification;
- substantial owner time and revenue-work disruption across multiple sessions;
- executed 2026-10-09 recurrence after the HIGH anti-loop controls were already in place;
- fresh credential state was restored and then immediately altered again by OS1 troubleshooting.

### Not proven
- no credential disclosure or hostile access;
- no eBay platform breach;
- no quantified financial loss;
- exact current credential state remains unverified.

### Company controls
- eBay API auth-dependent writes: HOLD;
- Issue #44 SOK execution: HOLD / preserved;
- no automatic “reauthorize/reset” response to 400/401/Trading/REST/state errors;
- classify the failed layer first;
- current-state evidence before every credential-affecting action;
- one reviewed action only; stop on first failure;
- owner is not the primary debugger.

Technical incident: https://github.com/elevationupscales/elevationupscales-elevation-agent-manager/issues/56  
Preserved SOK execution: https://github.com/elevationupscales/elevationupscales-elevation-agent-manager/issues/44

This PR updates the internal Recon Damage Report and current project incident state only. No credential values, eBay mutations, customer actions, or deployments are included.

Fixes the bug inline code is invisible in dark mode (near-black text on near-black background).

## Cause

- Inline code is styled by `@uncinq/css-base` with `color: var(--code-color-text, var(--color-text-on-muted))` and `background-color: var(--color-color-background, var(--color-background-muted))`.
- The dark theme of `@uncinq/design-tokens@1.8.3` (pinned in `yarn.lock`) remaps `--color-background-muted` to `--color-gray-900` in `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)`, but does **not** remap `--color-text-on-muted`, which keeps its light-mode value `--color-gray-900`.
- Result: gray-900 text on gray-900 background → invisible inline code (and same issue for `kbd`, `status`, `avatars`, `push-card`, `keyfeatures` which use text-on-muted on muted backgrounds).
- Newer `@uncinq/design-tokens` releases fix this upstream by adding `--color-text-on-muted: var(--color-gray-200)` to the dark theme.

## Fix (site-level, no Hugolify repo touched)

In `assets/css/site.css` (the design-system override file, imported last by `css/main.css`), remap the token in dark mode with the same selector upstream uses:

```css
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root:not([data-color-scheme="light"]) {
    --color-text-on-muted: var(--color-gray-200);
  }
}
```

This also fixes `kbd` keys and other text-on-muted components in dark mode, and is harmless once `@uncinq/design-tokens` is updated (same value as upstream).

> Pas de preview par PR sur ce dépôt : pour tester localement, `hugo server -D` avec le thème sombre du navigateur (ou `data-color-scheme`).

## Objetivo

Completar el primer criterio del issue #17: capturar y firmar el `ProviderResult` original emitido por el Core, sin reconstruir confianza desde el DTO del navegador.

## Cambios

- callback solo de servidor tras completar y limitar por dominio los resultados `auditIssues` y `auditPages`;
- valida marca de confianza del Core, proveedor, operación y mismo `auditId` en provenance;
- firma ambos resultados con el contexto UUID organización/proyecto;
- rechaza copias JSON y cruces entre auditorías;
- un fallo de captura queda separado del estado de OpenSEO y no oculta el informe terminado;
- documentación ADR, ROADMAP y HANDOFF.

## Verificación local

- 187/187 pruebas;
- 70/70 pruebas dirigidas OpenSEO/UI;
- pin, secretos, lint, TypeScript y diff correctos;
- el build local conserva el bloqueo conocido `ENOENT uv_resident_set_memory`; queda a cargo de CI.

No escribe en Supabase ni activa persistencia: la transacción idempotente, jobs y migración siguen pendientes. Sin secretos, llamadas live, funciones de pago ni cambios en Sarah.

Adds an optional online synchronous delivery mode to the curriculum design tool.

- Optional `delivery_mode` field and `toledo_h07` block carrying the 9 canonical stages of Toledo EQ-002/H.07.v1.
- Validator rules:
  - trace-only evidence is rejected outside ZoomState/Barrier stages;
  - outcome stages must use a performance-type evidence kind;
  - an AI endorser is rejected;
  - assisted performance is not treated as unaided;
  - a warning is raised when outcome numbers appear in prose.
- Adds a fictional demo5 example.
- Adds 46 stdlib-only tests.
- Demos 1-4 are byte-identical to before.

Note: H.07 is a Toledo Definition (a composition of stages), not a validated causal law.

SEO PR 2b, after #402: the `path` that answers still left null where the answer lacked what makes one. No bump.

**Members by their slug.** A member named by its `member_key` alone now has `/leden/<slug>`:
- the votes of members on a decision (`/api/decisions/{key}`, `/{key}/document`, the decisions of `/api/documents/{key}`);
- submitters of a motion or amendment (`/api/documents/{key}`);
- signatories on a dossier's timeline;
- persons of an item in the feed;
- members of a commitment (`/api/commitments`, `/api/commitments/{key}`);
- the prime minister of a cabinet and its bewindspersonen (`/api/cabinets`, `/api/cabinets/{key}`).

The slugs come from one map, `load_member_slugs` (`db/queries/committees.py`). It is kept per data version of `members`, and it is a warm-up part (`member slugs`).

**Papers in search.** A paper in a search hit now has `/kamerstukken/36600-VIII/5`: the query gives its dossier number, suffix, sequence and number along.

**How.** The props that make the address are passed to the DTO in a hidden field, `path_props` (`WithPath`, not in the answer or its schema). The raw rows of the queries keep their shape. A member without a slug, or a summary of the feed (no slug map), still has null.

**Still null:** a publication without its `official_id` (references to instruments outside the list), left for later.

**Docs:** api.md, the node row: a decision has a path since #402.

**Tests:**
- `tests/test_readable_paths_in_answers.py`:
  - a vote of a member by its slug;
  - a vote of a faction;
  - a submitter without a slug gets none;
  - a paper in a search hit by its suffix;
  - `path_props` is not in the answer.
- `tests/api/conftest.py` stubs the slug map. The vote in `test_parliamentary_api.py` has its faction's path.
- `tests/pg/test_feed_queries.py`, `tests/test_feed.py`: the persons have `path`.
- `tests/pg/test_query_plans.py`: the slug map reads all of `members` by design (`_WHOLE_BY_DESIGN`).
- `tests/integration/test_motion_titles.py`, `test_government_api.py`: submitters, the prime minister and the member of a commitment by their slug (`/leden/m-faber`, `/leden/eelco-heinen`).
- Green: mypy, unit (4,152), the full tests/pg (948, before the cabinets commit; the cabinet, render and plan files again after it), and the 26 integration files that read the changed routes (after it).

